         <div type="bio">
            <p>Irish actress who began her career at the Abbey Theatre and gained popularity with her roles in <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Sean O’Casey</name>’s plays. Her film career included roles in several early Hitchcock films. At the 14th Academy Awards, she was nominated for Best Supporting Actress for her role in <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">How Green Was My Valley</name>. She became an American citizen in 1945. Allgood was rumored to have planned a reading in London of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Anna Livia Plurabelle</name> in September 1932. <hi rend="bold">Geert Lernout</hi> and <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
